Source: vintner-boot
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: zcomputerwiz <zcomputerwiz@users.noreply.github.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), golang-go (>= 2:1.24~),
 binutils, ca-certificates, cpio, curl, kmod, xz-utils,
 grub-pc-bin, systemd-boot-efi
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: vintner-core
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, sbsigntool, systemd-boot-efi, systemd-ukify
Recommends: plymouth, plymouth-themes
Description: vintner boot platform - core tools, publisher and health checks
 Common boot metadata schema, manifest validation, state model, CLI and
 API. Contains the publisher (kernel and initramfs hooks, image build,
 verification and signing, atomic staging and garbage collection), the
 health checks and the bless service for both firmware backends.

Package: vintner-platform
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Conflicts: systemd-boot, grub-pc, grub-efi-amd64, shim-signed, grub-cloud-amd64,
 grub-efi-ia32, grub-coreboot, grub-xen, grub-ieee1275, refind
Description: vintner boot platform - inert boot loader and recovery payloads
 Platform payloads installed under /usr/lib/vintner/payloads/: the
 systemd-boot and systemd-stub binaries, the GRUB BIOS boot sector and
 modules, and the recovery kernel and initramfs. Installing or upgrading
 this package never touches the ESP, boot storage or NVRAM; deploying a
 payload is an explicit act of the installer.

Package: vintner-installer
Architecture: all
Description: vintner boot platform - installation integration
 Guided and automated installation integration: partition setup,
 firmware probe and boot entry registration. A udeb follows later.
